{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1339249-older-books-that-are-still-super-useful","id":1339249,"title":"older books that are still super useful","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-10-03T15:14:08-07:00","id":1339249,"title":"older books that are still super useful","content":"I was looking to compile a general list of older werewolf books (1st ed on through revised) that are still quite useful to a 20th anniversary Storyteller. Basically things that haven't been made completely redundant by the books published so far (examples of redundant books are the previous books of the wyrm, player's guide to the changing breeds, ways of the wolf, Umbra, etc). <br /> - The Chronicle of the Black Labyrinth, and Silver Record: Two in setting books that are full of great flavor and story seeds. I've used the Silver Record as a great in character way to provide pc Galliards with readings for moots.<br /> - Werewolf Chronicles vol 1: I call special attention to vol 1 rather than 2 because, while monkeywrench is a great book, ways of the wolf is very dated and now rendered obsolete by Changing Ways. Vol 1 has two books, Rite of Passage, and Valkenburg Foundation. Both are story supplements, providing ready made adventures easily plopped into any chronicle. I have used Rite of Passage as a first adventure for at least 3 groups of PCs, each of which ended very differently. Valkenburg is a great sequel to Rite of Passage, being a series of individual stories that can be used in between your own stories.<br /> - Rage Across the Heavens - High renown play at it's most bizarre. a wild ride through the myriad planetary Umbral realms.<br /> - Past Lives - another pre written adventure, this time through a dark umbral reflection of some of the garou's greatest failures. a great way to start a chronicle that could very easily provide a prelude to the usage of Shattered Dreams.<br /> - Croatan Song - Did i mention Shattered Dreams and Past lives being time travel type stories? Well this makes for a great supplement to provide an extended stay in the deep past of what would become north america. <br /> - The various Setting books (Rage Acroos Yadda Yadda, and Dark Alliance Vancouver): I have used most of these as examples of places and transported their story hooks into my home game, but if you want a place to set your story, i have found these are generally pretty good. <br /> <br /> Have i missed any of the super useful older books? These are merely the ones I've found useful thus far in constructing and maintaining a campaign. I'm sure there are more that people are using a regular basis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2778-tlalchitonatiuh","name":"Tlalchitonatiuh","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-03T17:16:56-07:00","id":1339266,"title":"","content":"Hammer &amp; Klave?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-03T17:21:10-07:00","id":1339269,"title":"","content":"The original Breed Books as I don't think any other printing (Changing Breeds) has gone into as much detail as the individual books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25442-tikank","name":"TIKank","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-03T17:23:25-07:00","id":1339270,"title":"","content":"Revised was treasure packed dream run. Only flop I can think of was the Children of Gaia tribebook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-03T17:47:11-07:00","id":1339273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1339249-older-books-that-are-still-super-useful?p=1339270#post1339270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Revised was treasure packed dream run. Only flop I can think of was the Children of Gaia tribebook.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I still use the original Tribe Books as I have them all. How different are the revised editions? I love the original and have never put up the $$$ to get the newer ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25442-tikank","name":"TIKank","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-03T18:00:19-07:00","id":1339274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TIKank</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1339249-older-books-that-are-still-super-useful?p=1339273#post1339273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I still use the original Tribe Books as I have them all. How different are the revised editions? I love the original and have never put up the $$$ to get the newer ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have half the revised and I\u2019ve found them to be Golden! I love the Get book! Children of Gaia has been universally panned, but It was suggested I read the first one. How was it? In revised the Children of Gaia seem to lack a solid concrete identity and history of find in the other books.<br /> <br /> Some tribebooks cover the whole tribes history and how they are in different regions and eras, but it\u2019s not uniform across the books so their method of covering the tribes vary. But I definitely got a more concrete understanding of say the Glass Walkers, Silverfangs and Uktena compared to the simple info given in the core. Like the explanation of the Silverfang houses, the idea that Uktena actually had a different totem, I think it was Sky Falcon, in prehistory but Uktena proved to be more clever and bested it so they followed the mysterious spirit instead and the explanation that the Glass Walkers have kind of a popular Subfaction each Era that reinvents the Tribe. Like before corporate Glasswalker Identity they were Mafioso Wolves, and before that they were Iron Riders that promoted Weaver progress, and in the Renaissance they were Alchemists and in the olden days of yore they were just the Warders of Men.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-03T18:03:22-07:00","id":1339275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TIKank</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1339249-older-books-that-are-still-super-useful?p=1339269#post1339269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The original Breed Books as I don't think any other printing (Changing Breeds) has gone into as much detail as the individual books.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very much so, the original books are key. The Changing 20 book however is really good and adds new details. Like we get the Ahafi fleshed out like they are a new Hengeyokai. And the Hengeyokai get some fleshing out. Before I didn\u2019t understand for instance what it meant when they took a Hengeyokai Auspice I thought they replaced your old one, but they explain they just add onto them if I remember correctly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-03T18:09:33-07:00","id":1339276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1339249-older-books-that-are-still-super-useful?p=1339274#post1339274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have half the revised and I\u2019ve found them to be Golden! I love the Get book! Children of Gaia has been universally panned, but It was suggested I read the first one. How was it? In revised the Children of Gaia seem to lack a solid concrete identity and history of find in the other books.<br /> <br /> Some tribebooks cover the whole tribes history and how they are in different regions and eras, but it\u2019s not uniform across the books so their method of covering the tribes vary. But I definitely got a more concrete understanding of say the Glass Walkers, Silverfangs and Uktena compared to the simple info given in the core. Like the explanation of the Silverfang houses, the idea that Uktena actually had a different totem, I think it was Sky Falcon, in prehistory but Uktena proved to be more clever and bested it so they followed the mysterious spirit instead and the explanation that the Glass Walkers have kind of a popular Subfaction each Era that reinvents the Tribe. Like before corporate Glasswalker Identity they were Mafioso Wolves, and before that they were Iron Riders that promoted Weaver progress, and in the Renaissance they were Alchemists and in the olden days of yore they were just the Warders of Men.</div> </div> </div> </div>The original Children of Gaia was meh. Not sure how it stacks up to the newest one, but it didn't make me like the tribe any more. The first Bone Gnawer tribe book was amazing though. When I read it, they became my favorite tribe. They have a ritual where they blackball your ass (Using an eight ball) and as long as you wear it, no other supernatural creature will deal with you. If you have never read it, read it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25442-tikank","name":"TIKank","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-03T18:19:01-07:00","id":1339278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tlalchitonatiuh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1339249-older-books-that-are-still-super-useful#post1339249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Basically things that haven't been made completely redundant by the books published so far (examples of redundant books are the previous books of the wyrm, player's guide to the changing breeds, ways of the wolf, Umbra, etc).</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, thinking about it, there are still a few reasons to get some of the 1e stuff. The 1e Book of the Wyrm had some REALLY messed up toys that were created for children in the last section. Seeing as WWtA 1e stuff is pretty cheap most of the time, I'd get them all. ;D","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25442,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25442-tikank","user":"TIKank","date":". 10-03-2019, 09:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25442-tikank","name":"TIKank","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-03T18:25:44-07:00","id":1339279,"title":"","content":"Damnit clicked preview and it erases my response! Damnit! I friggin hat typing on the phone!<br /> <br /> <br /> I missed out on the original tribe books because I hopped on at Revised. I wishe I got them at the devil made me do it sale a decade and a half ago where they sold their inventory at $6.66 a book.<br /> <br /> I loved the 1st Ed\u2019s I did read though, love Rage Across Russia.<br /> <br /> Rage Across Egypt and Rage Across the Heavens were also brilliant and fun even if you don\u2019t plan to visit in game they are full of ideas. But everyone can hold a game in the Aetherial realm so have your pack go there!<br /> <br /> Umbra Revised was probably pound for pound my most favorite Whitewolf book! I got so much use out of it and it sparked my imagination into a blaze as a wee lad!<br /> <br /> The revised Bonegnawers book was great for helping understand the tribe. It explains how the tribe has loose standard and a lot of Garou not wanting responsibility join so you get a bunch of dudes who stay at rank 1 or maybe 2 their whole lives. But since they are twice as big as other tribes they still have just as many true heroes as the other more vaunted tribes. And it even goes into the old Osirian league days were Sutekh cursed them with some sort of Jackal Curse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}